</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">These results validate our skeleton construction approach, with negative correlations confirming that lift increases as model confidence (decreasing entropy) increases, providing the foundation for meaningful stopping decisions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Grid Analysis</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our mixture e-process construction relies on a carefully designed parameter grid that balances computational efficiency with approximation quality. We employ log-spaced construction with <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}=0.02\cdot 2^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}=0.02\cdot 2^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,K</annotation></semantics></math>, covering the range <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.02,0.6]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.02</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.02,0.6]</annotation></semantics></math> which remains safely below the theoretical bound <math id="A6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/c\approx 5.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>5.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/c\approx 5.5</annotation></semantics></math> for our estimated parameter <math id="A6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=0.18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=0.18</annotation></semantics></math>. This exponential spacing ensures adequate coverage of both small and large parameter values while maintaining computational tractability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Empirical evaluation of grid approximation quality demonstrates that our choice of <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=12</annotation></semantics></math> provides excellent performance relative to hindsight-optimal parameter selection. The following table shows the fraction of sequences where our grid achieves performance within specified multiples of the hindsight-optimal <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Grid approximation quality (fraction within multiples of optimal <math id="A6.T12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>).</figcaption>
<div id="A6.T12.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:169.1pt;height:29.4pt;vertical-align:-13.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-56.7pt,9.9pt) scale(0.598592487202968,0.598592487202968) ;">
<table id="A6.T12.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A6.T12.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A6.T12.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Grid <math id="A6.T12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="A6.T12.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A6.T12.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Within 2×</span></th>
<th id="A6.T12.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A6.T12.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Within 1.5×</span></th>
<th id="A6.T12.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A6.T12.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Avg regret/tok</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A6.T12.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">6</th>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">87.1%</td>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">67.8%</td>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.045</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">12</th>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">96.2%</td>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">83.9%</td>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.019</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">16</th>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">98.1%</td>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">89.3%</td>
<td id="A6.T12.2.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.013</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These results confirm that <math id="A6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=12</annotation></semantics></math> provides excellent approximation quality, achieving performance within 2× of optimal for 96.2% of sequences while maintaining reasonable computational overhead. The diminishing returns beyond <math id="A6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=12</annotation></semantics></math> justify our parameter choice for practical deployment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Skip Predictor Validation</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We validate our entropy-slope skip predictor through systematic comparison with alternative features on held-out data, training logistic regression models to predict when information lift computation is worthwhile (specifically, <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbbm{1}\{X_{t}&gt;0.5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbbm{1}\{X_{t}&gt;0.5\}</annotation></semantics></math>). Our feature set encompasses entropy-slope (<math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t-1}-H_{t-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t-1}-H_{t-2}</annotation></semantics></math>), perplexity (<math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(H_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(H_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>), attention-max (<math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j}\text{attn}_{t-1,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mtext>attn</mtext><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j}\text{attn}_{t-1,j}</annotation></semantics></math>), and token frequency (<math id="A7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\text{count}(y_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext>count</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\text{count}(y_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>), each capturing different aspects of model confidence and token predictability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The validation results on GSM8K demonstrate that entropy-slope provides the strongest single predictor for identifying tokens worth computing, achieving 0.82 AUC with only 2.1% skip failures compared to alternatives like perplexity (0.76 AUC, 3.4% failures) and attention-max (0.71 AUC, 4.2% failures). While a multi-feature logistic regression achieves slightly better performance (0.85 AUC, 1.7% failures), the marginal improvement comes at significant complexity cost, leading us to adopt entropy-slope for its simplicity and strong empirical performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Skip predictor validation on GSM8K (<math id="A7.T13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=500</annotation></semantics></math>). AUC for predicting <math id="A7.T13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}&gt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}&gt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<div id="A7.T13.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:169.1pt;height:52.2pt;vertical-align:-24.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-34.6pt,10.7pt) scale(0.709495449367258,0.709495449367258) ;">
